god_exists	one
infinite_good	two	infinite	P2	goodness as a contrary is unbounded in extent, pervading everything so that no room is left for its opposite	God's own goodness is unlimited in degree or perfection, as an attribute of one being
evil	one
# infinite_good: S1 needs "infinite" to mean that the good fills all things, which would leave no room for evil.
# S2 gets "infinite goodness" from what "God" means, which is boundless perfection in God himself; that does not by itself imply the good occupies the whole world.
# I was unsure whether the text means this shift. I mark it two because each sense would be made true by something different.
